            "review_title": "Review at Heritage Coffee Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Jonathan H\nLondon, United Kingdom133 contributions\n0\nNot great\nMar 2017 • Solo\nCame in here and reaching the Citadel entrance and realising I was going to self-digest unless I had some lunch - nothing else nearby. The garden looks appealing, but there is a lot of traffic noise so it's not exactly a calming environment. The menu's English translations are a little off - they have \"synthetic olives\" and \"synthetic dried fruits\" on there, and god only knows what they're meant to be. Also note that where everything comes with \"eat with fried tomatoes\", they do actually mean French fries. I had the club sandwich, which consisted of four slices of slightly soggy white bread with various layers, each smothered in pink mayonnaise that tasted rather like strawberry milk. After one attempted bite at eating this like an actual sandwich, I resorted to knife and fork. The fries were OK though. Sandwich and a Pepsi came to 100,000VND, which is about £3.50 I think. Toilets are a bit grim, wifi works well.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten March 12, 2017",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
