            "review_text": "stanthombre1\nLondon, United Kingdom4 contributions\n0\nWorst place we ate at- by a long distance\nFeb 2017 • Couples\nIt always feels bad giving a negative review- it was possibly us that were caught out, having walked for miles and simply popping in the first coffee shop we saw. \n\nThe food was poor and the service slow. We felt under pressure to order, as the waiter hovered over us as we poured through the menu. We ordered a couple of lunch time sandwiches. My partner's club sandwich had hard, inedible meat that was quickly discarded. The chips were cold (admittedly not a Vietnamese speciality!) and we had to wait 45 minutes for two rather basic sandwiches in an empty restaurant.\n\nI suppose we could say this was the only time we didn't have Vietnamese food and were caught out. But be warned- it is much better to carry on walking and stop off in another one of the fine eateries (Banh Mi's are the way forward, people!) along the way. To be avoided.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 4, 2017",
